src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol:joinPoolAndStake|class=C22|Medium|msgValue = _amounts[ethIndex] followed by unconditional WETH.withdraw(msgValue) presumes the ETH-leg amount is currently held as WETH, but _executeDepositTrades buys that leg with buyToken = address(tokens[i]) = ETH_ADDRESS, so the trading module delivers native ETH and the vault holds no matching WETH — the unwrap either reverts (deposit-trade entry permanently unusable on every ETH-legged pool whose asset is not the ETH leg) or, when unrelated WETH is present in the vault, unwraps that other bucket and leaves an equal amount of native ETH stranded outside the LP accounting.|src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol
